WHAT THIS IS

The browser capture the visual-proof rule asks for, produced in CI by
.github/workflows/chat-visual-proof.yml against a stack booted from
refs/pull/1769/merge on a hosted runner, with that run's own Supabase, its own
registered OAuth client and a real streamed completion. The session is minted
through the real "Continue with Hive" journey, not stubbed.

The account is an ordinary one, and this run is the first that can say so
honestly. See the section at the bottom: three earlier green captures were taken
as an instance admin, which proved the surface works and proved nothing about
the permission this issue grants. The capture now reads the session's own role
and refuses anything but `user`, so the claim is measured rather than argued.

WHAT IT SHOWS, IN ORDER

  01-signed-in          the signed-in chat surface, session live, role `user`
  01b-project-created   POST /api/v1/knowledge/create answered 200, and the
                        browser is on the new project's page
  01c-document-added    the uploaded document listed on that project
  02-model-picker       the alias the turn will run on, hive-free
  03-streamed-reply     the answer, 47
  04-sources-expanded   the source list, naming kb-1505-field-note.txt

The document's fact is invented, so a correct answer cannot be recall. The
source list is required outright on top of it: an answer with no rendered
source would prove the document was read somewhere, not that the surface told
the customer where from.

The images are on the visual-proof-assets release and are linked from the pull
request, per .wolf/decisions.md D-042. This file is the text half, committed
here because npm run lint:proof-tokens scans docs/proof/ and nothing else.

