TWO RED RUNS CAME FIRST, AND BOTH ARE THE POINT

Run 33711437643 failed with "creating a knowledge base answered 500". The
security hardening had added a group-grant filter call to knowledge.py that
passed `db`, a local the create route deliberately does not have. The patch
applied cleanly, the module parsed, the marker counts matched and every unit
assertion passed. Only this capture went red.
scripts/test_owui_skill_group_grants.py now carries a structural guard that
refuses any inserted call naming a name the enclosing function has not bound
above it.

Run 33715826859 failed with "the capturing account's role is admin, not user".
That assertion had just been added at a reviewer's request, and it went red on
its first run. owui.setup.ts promotes the fixture to Open WebUI instance admin
so it can install the JWT-forward Function, the capture reuses that same
session, and the promotion is undone only by the account's next login, which
never happens inside a run. So the three green captures before it, 33710378904,
33712312976 and their predecessor, were all admin captures: they show the
surface working and say nothing about the permission, because an admin passes
the gate this issue is about. The promotion script now takes the role to write,
and the projects scenario hands the role back before capturing.

Both defects were found by an assertion added in review, not by the code it
guards, and neither was visible to any static check.
